+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time to a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit: `d` (days), `h` (hours),
+`m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once and in that order, without spaces, for example
+`2d`, `1h30m`, `90m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Units are case-insensitive. Negative and decimal values are rejected.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=120"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1.5h"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--help"])
+```
+
